From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:31:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: support Venus implicit native dma-bufs

A paired Metal renderer without DRM format modifiers shares an optimal image
as the native MTLHeap that backs it, and the dma-buf then names that
allocation, not a layout. Guest Zink imports such a DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID
dma-buf as the same optimal image over the same heap: it keeps the image
optimal, withholds host-image-copy usage, which could change the Metal layout,
reports the logical stride of the window system's envelope, and releases
ownership to the external queue family where the renderer has no
VK_EXT_queue_family_foreign.

Venus common WSI makes the matching share under the same condition. Its
swapchain images stay on the direct scanout path, bounded by the renderer's
per-image budget, with the logical row pitch the implicit envelope needs
supplied only through the private WSI layout query, and a virtio-mmio DRM node
is recognized as the device itself so that Xwayland's DRI3 fd does not force a
PRIME copy.

A renderer with DRM format modifiers names the layout it shares. Zink then
shares every image as DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR and reads an implicit import as
linear, as upstream Venus does, so Venus WSI offers the modifiers and takes
the explicit-modifier path, or its linear prime blit, rather than an implicit
native share that an importer would read as linear rows. The Venus predicate is
a header-only helper the native test covers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
